      "resource": "azurerm_linux_function_app.alert_function",
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "explanation": "The azurerm_linux_function_app resource does not explicitly disable public network access, potentially exposing the Function App to unauthorized access."
    }
  ],
  "patched_code": ```hcl
resource "azurerm_linux_function_app" "alert_function" {
  name                = "smart-manufacturing-iot-monitoring-platform-function-app-alerts"
  resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.smart_manufacturing.name
  location            = azurerm_resource_group.smart_manufacturing.location
  service_plan_id     = azurerm_service_plan.dashboard_plan.id
  storage_account_name       = azurerm_storage_account.function_storage.name
  storage_account_access_key = azurerm_storage_account.function_storage.primary_access_key
  site_config {
    application_stack {
      node_version = "18"
    }
    https_only = true
  }
  app_settings = {
    "FUNCTIONS_WORKER_RUNTIME" = "node"
  }
}
```,
  "fix_summary": "Added 'https_only = true' to the site_config block to enforce HTTPS-only access. However, the 'public_network_access_enabled' attribute is not available in the azurerm_linux_function_app resource. It is recommended to check the AzureRM provider documentation for the correct attribute or version that supports disabling public network access."
